import { company } from "../../data/company";
---

<p>
  At {company.legalName} we want you to feel safe when you visit us online. Here you can read how we use cookies, which personal
  data we collect, why we collect it and how we look after it.
</p>

<h2>1. Introduction</h2>
<p>When you visit mistermellow.dk, we collect information about your visit in order to:</p>
<ul>
  <li>tailor and improve the content of the site</li>
  <li>make our marketing more relevant to you</li>
  <li>give you a better and smoother experience</li>
</ul>
<p>If you don't want us to collect this information, you can delete or block cookies (see section 4) and stop using the site.</p>

<h2>2. What are cookies?</h2>
<p>A cookie is a small text file stored on your computer, tablet or phone when you visit a website. Cookies are used to:</p>
<ul>
  <li>recognise you when you come back</li>
  <li>remember your choices and settings</li>
  <li>collect statistics so we can improve the site</li>
  <li>show you ads and content that suit you</li>
</ul>
<p>A cookie cannot contain viruses or other harmful code. It simply makes it easier for your browser and our site to talk to each other.</p>

<h2>3. How we use cookies</h2>
<p>We use both our own cookies (first-party) and cookies from partners (third-party) for three purposes:</p>
<h3>Functional cookies</h3>
<p>Make the site work and remember your choices – for example that you have confirmed your age and what you have put in your cart.</p>
<h3>Statistical cookies</h3>
<p>
  Help us understand how the site is used so we can improve content and features. For this we may use Google Analytics or a
  similar tool that shows which pages are visited and for how long.
</p>
<h3>Marketing cookies</h3>
<p>Used by us and our partners to make ads more relevant and to make sure you don't see the same ad over and over.</p>

<h2>4. How to delete or block cookies</h2>
<p>
  You can delete or block cookies in your browser at any time. See a guide (in Danish) at
  <a href="https://minecookies.org/cookiehandtering" target="_blank" rel="noopener">minecookies.org/cookiehandtering</a>.
</p>
<p>
  Please note that the site may not work as intended if you block or delete cookies. You may also see ads that are less relevant
  and appear more often.
</p>

<h2>5. What personal data do we collect?</h2>
<p>When you use the site, we collect two kinds of information:</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    <strong>Information that cannot be traced back to you:</strong> for example your IP address, browser type, technical details
    about your device, your approximate location and which pages you click on.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Information that can be traced back to you:</strong> the information you give us yourself with your consent – for
    example when you shop, sign up for a newsletter or contact us. This may be your name, email, phone number, address and payment
    details.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>6. Security</h2>
<p>
  We process your data in line with applicable law, including the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and the Danish Data
  Protection Act. Your data is treated confidentially, and we have technical and organisational safeguards that protect it from
  being deleted, altered, disclosed, misused or seen by unauthorised persons.
</p>

<h2>7. Why do we collect data?</h2>
<ul>
  <li>To recognise you and give you a more personal experience on the site.</li>
  <li>To deliver what you ask for – such as your orders, newsletters and competitions.</li>
  <li>To make the site better and easier to use, partly based on statistics about how it is used.</li>
  <li>To show you ads that are relevant to you.</li>
</ul>

<h2>8. How long do we keep the data?</h2>
<p>
  We only keep your personal data for as long as we need it for the purposes above, or for as long as the law requires – for
  example the Danish Bookkeeping Act. How long depends on the type of information and why we have it. When we no longer need the
  information, we delete or anonymise it.
</p>

<h2>9. Who do we share data with?</h2>
<p>
  We may share information about how you use the site – for example which ads you see and click on, your approximate location,
  gender and age group – with our advertising partners, where this information is available. This is done so you see more relevant
  ads. Read more in section 3.
</p>
<p>
  We also use external suppliers (data processors) to store and process data, for example for hosting, payments and shipping. They
  may only use the data on our behalf and according to our instructions – never for their own purposes. We only share your name and
  email if you have explicitly agreed to it. We only use suppliers within the EU or in countries that protect data as well as the EU.
</p>

<h2>10. Your rights</h2>
<p>You always have the right to:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Access:</strong> find out what information we hold about you.</li>
  <li><strong>Rectification:</strong> have incorrect or incomplete information corrected.</li>
  <li><strong>Erasure:</strong> have your information deleted when we no longer have a legitimate need for it.</li>
  <li><strong>Restriction:</strong> in certain cases, have the processing of your information restricted.</li>
  <li><strong>Objection:</strong> object to the processing – especially when it comes to direct marketing.</li>
  <li><strong>Data portability:</strong> receive your information in a structured, commonly used and machine-readable format.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  If you want to use your rights or have questions about how we process your data, email
  <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a>.
</p>
<p>
  If you are unhappy with how we process your data, you can complain to the Danish Data Protection Agency,
  <a href="https://www.datatilsynet.dk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Datatilsynet</a>.
</p>

